Code generation: install the templates as data (share/acado/templates)

The code generator reads its templates (*.in) at run time, from the
installed include/acado/code_generation/templates. Installed with the
headers, they are packaged with them, in acado-dev: on a target with only
acado, exportCode() could not open acado_auxiliary_functions.h.in and
wrote an incomplete solver. Install them as data, to share/acado/templates,
and look for them there (templates.hpp, the header naming the directory,
stays with the headers).

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/acado/code_generation/templates/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/acado/code_generation/templates/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 #
 
 SET( INSTALL_TEMPLATE_PATH
-	${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/${INSTALL_INCLUDE_DIR}/code_generation/templates
+	${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/${INSTALL_DATA_DIR}/templates
 )
 
 IF( CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING )
@@ -105,8 +105,15 @@
 
 INSTALL(
 	FILES
-		${TEMPLATES}
 		"${CG_TEMPLATES_PATH}/templates.hpp"
 	DESTINATION
 		${INSTALL_INCLUDE_DIR}/code_generation/templates
 )
+# The templates are what the code generator reads at run time: data, not
+# headers.
+INSTALL(
+	FILES
+		${TEMPLATES}
+	DESTINATION
+		${INSTALL_DATA_DIR}/templates
+)
